---
/**
 * TerraformPlanSummarizerPlayground — the terraform-plan-summarizer island.
 *
 * Paste `terraform plan` output (or `terraform show -json`) and get the four
 * numbers that matter, the resources behind them, and — the part no other plan
 * reader does — a cross-check of the parsed list against Terraform's own "Plan:"
 * line, in which each replacement counts once as an add AND once as a destroy.
 * When the two disagree the tool says so loudly instead of printing a confident
 * wrong total.
 *
 * Ported from `CidrCheckerPlayground.astro` (the contract reference): example
 * chips at `var(--radius-pill)`, one debounce plus a 600 ms calm-error hold, the
 * exact run hint line, per-row copy plus `data-copy-all`, one visible
 * `role="status"` summary and one sr-only copy status, NO `aria-live` on the
 * results container, `escapeHtml()` on every injected value (attributes
 * included), and the two coarse-pointer tap-target tiers.
 *
 * FOUR DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS, each with a reason:
 *
 *  1. **No deep link, and no `data-copy-link` at all.** Plans run 5,000–50,000
 *     lines; the smallest useful one is already past the ~2,000-character
 *     fragment cap every other tool here respects. Nothing in this file reads or
 *     writes `location.hash`. The share affordance is "Copy summary as Markdown"
 *     carrying `data-copy-all` — PR-comment shaped, which is where a plan review
 *     actually happens. It already emits `result_copied` through Layout.astro's
 *     listener, so analytics is unaffected.
 *
 *  2. **Plain textarea, no CodeMirror.** Syntax highlighting a 50,000-line log
 *     costs ~150 KB of editor for zero information (certificate-decoder and
 *     chmod-calculator set the same precedent). Input is capped at 2 MiB with a
 *     note that says exactly how many characters were dropped.
 *
 *  3. **The stat band shows four DISJOINT tiles**, not Terraform's overlapping
 *     add/change/destroy. `+ add` is resources created outright and `± replace`
 *     is resources destroyed and recreated — a replacement is never counted in
 *     both tiles. Terraform's own accounting is printed underneath, verbatim, so
 *     neither number can be mistaken for the other.
 *
 *  4. **No cost estimate, permanently.** Pricing goes stale and a stale figure
 *     printed with confidence is the one mistake this site cannot make.
 *
 * Runtime contract (lazy-imported inside the boot closure so the engine and its
 * fixtures code-split away from the page shell):
 *   ../lib/terraform-plan-summarizer/engine → summarizePlan, toMarkdown,
 *                                             formatTerraformTotals
 */
import { examples } from '../lib/terraform-plan-summarizer/examples';
---

<section class="tps-pg" aria-label="Terraform plan summarizer playground">
  <div class="card shadow-float overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
    {/* ── Example chips ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 border-b border-hairline px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
      <span class="eyebrow">Examples</span>
      <div id="tps-chips" class="tps-chips" role="group" aria-label="Examples">
        {
          examples.map((ex, i) => (
            <button type="button" class="tps-chip" data-example-idx={String(i)} aria-pressed="false">
              {ex.label}
            </button>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* ── Input ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <div class="border-b border-hairline px-4 py-4 sm:px-5">
      <label class="eyebrow mb-2 block" for="tps-input">Plan output</label>
      <textarea
        id="tps-input"
        class="tps-input code-mono"
        spellcheck="false"
        autocapitalize="off"
        autocorrect="off"
        autocomplete="off"
        rows="12"
        placeholder="Terraform will perform the following actions:&#10;&#10;  # aws_db_instance.primary must be replaced&#10;-/+ resource &quot;aws_db_instance&quot; &quot;primary&quot; {&#10;      ~ engine_version = &quot;13.4&quot; -&gt; &quot;15.3&quot; # forces replacement&#10;    }&#10;&#10;Plan: 1 to add, 0 to change, 1 to destroy."
        aria-describedby="tps-input-hint tps-run-hint"></textarea>
      <p id="tps-input-hint" class="tps-hint caption text-mute">
        Both formats work and the format is detected for you: the human-readable
        <span class="code-mono">terraform plan</span> transcript (ANSI colour codes and CRLF from a
        CI log are fine) or <span class="code-mono">terraform show -json tfplan</span>. Up to 2 MiB
        — roughly a 50,000-line plan. It stays in this tab: there is no server here to send it to,
        which matters, because plan output is full of account IDs, ARNs, CIDRs and policy JSON.
      </p>
      <p id="tps-run-hint" class="tps-hint caption text-mute">Results update as you type — press Enter to run now.</p>

      <div class="tps-control">
        <span class="eyebrow" id="tps-group-label">Grouping</span>
        <div class="tps-seg" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="tps-group-label">
          <button
            id="tps-group-action"
            type="button"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="true"
            tabindex="0"
            class="tps-seg__btn code-mono"
          >
            By action
          </button>
          <button
            id="tps-group-module"
            type="button"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="false"
            tabindex="-1"
            class="tps-seg__btn code-mono"
          >
            By module
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="tps-gloss caption text-mute">
          By action puts replacements and destroys first, because those are the ones that can take
          something down. By module follows the code instead, which is what you want when one
          module call is the thing under review.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tps-snap-row mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <button id="tps-snap-save" type="button" class="tps-snap-btn">Save snapshot</button>
        <select id="tps-snap-select" class="tps-snap-select" aria-label="Load a saved snapshot" disabled>
          <option value="">No snapshots yet</option>
        </select>
        <button id="tps-snap-delete" type="button" class="tps-snap-delete" aria-label="Delete this snapshot" hidden>&times;</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* ── Results ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <div class="bg-canvas-soft px-4 py-4 sm:px-5">
      <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
        <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          <span class="eyebrow">Result</span>
          <button
            id="tps-copy-md"
            type="button"
            class="tps-copy tps-copy--labeled"
            data-copy-all
            data-copy=""
            data-copy-label="Copy summary as Markdown"
            hidden
          >
            <svg
              class="tps-copy-icon"
              width="13"
              height="13"
              viewBox="0 0 16 16"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <rect x="5" y="5" width="9" height="9" rx="1.5"></rect>
              <path d="M3 11H2a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V2a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h8a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1"></path>
            </svg>
            <svg
              class="tps-check-icon hidden"
              width="13"
              height="13"
              viewBox="0 0 16 16"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <path d="M3 8.5l3.5 3.5L13 4.5"></path>
            </svg>
            <span class="tps-copy-label">Copy summary as Markdown</span>
          </button>
        </span>
        <span id="tps-summary" class="tps-summary code-mono text-mute" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>
      <div id="tps-results" class="tps-results">
        <p class="tps-empty body-sm text-mute">
          Paste a plan to see adds, changes, destroys and replacements counted separately, the
          replacement-forcing attributes named, and the totals cross-checked against Terraform&rsquo;s
          own summary line.
        </p>
      </div>
      <span id="tps-copy-status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @reference "../styles/global.css";

  /* ── Example chips ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tps-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    min-height: 26px;
  }
  .tps-chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    color: var(--color-brand-strong);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.12s ease, box-shadow 0.12s ease;
  }
  .tps-chip:hover,
  .tps-chip[aria-pressed='true'] {
    background: var(--color-brand-soft);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-brand);
  }
  .tps-chip:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-link);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  /* ── Input ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tps-input {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 260px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 19px;
    resize: vertical;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow: auto;
    transition: box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }
  .tps-input::placeholder {
    color: var(--color-mute);
  }
  .tps-input:hover {
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-hairline-strong);
  }
  .tps-input:focus {
    outline: none;
  }
  .tps-input:focus-visible {
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--color-link);
    outline: none;
  }
  .tps-input--error {
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-error);
  }
  .tps-hint {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .tps-hint + .tps-hint {
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .tps-hint .code-mono {
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  /* ── Grouping control ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tps-control {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }
  .tps-seg {
    display: inline-flex;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: 2px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-canvas-soft-2);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
  }
  .tps-seg__btn {
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 16px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
    touch-action: manipulation;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .tps-seg__btn:hover {
    color: var(--color-body);
  }
  .tps-seg__btn[aria-checked='true'] {
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
  }
  .tps-seg__btn:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-link);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  .tps-gloss {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* ── Snapshot row (same shape as every other playground) ─────────────── */
  .tps-snap-btn {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    height: 30px;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: none;
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    color: var(--color-body);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.12s ease, box-shadow 0.12s ease;
  }
  .tps-snap-btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-canvas-soft);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-hairline-strong);
  }
  .tps-snap-select {
    height: 30px;
    max-width: 220px;
    padding: 0 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    color: var(--color-body);
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }
  .tps-snap-select:disabled {
    color: var(--color-mute);
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .tps-snap-delete {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.12s ease, color 0.12s ease;
  }
  .tps-snap-delete:hover {
    background: var(--color-error-soft);
    color: var(--color-error-deep);
  }

  .tps-summary {
    min-width: 0;
    text-align: right;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .tps-results {
    min-height: 44px;
  }
  .tps-copy-status--fail {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    color: var(--color-error-deep);
  }

  /* ── Runtime-injected: stat band ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  :global(.tps-stats) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 560px) {
    :global(.tps-stats) {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  :global(.tps-stat) {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 10px 12px 11px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--color-hairline-strong);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--add) {
    border-top-color: var(--color-brand);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--change) {
    border-top-color: var(--color-accent-ink);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--destroy) {
    border-top-color: var(--color-error);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--replace) {
    border-top-color: var(--color-warning);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat__n) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 26px;
  }
  :global(.tps-stat__sym) {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--add .tps-stat__n) {
    color: var(--color-success);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--change .tps-stat__n) {
    color: var(--color-accent-ink);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--destroy .tps-stat__n) {
    color: var(--color-error-deep);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat--replace .tps-stat__n) {
    color: var(--color-warning-deep);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat__label) {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }
  :global(.tps-stat__sub) {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 16px;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  :global(.tps-tf-line) {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* ── Runtime-injected: blocks + rows ─────────────────────────────────── */
  :global(.tps-block) {
    margin-top: 12px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  :global(.tps-block__head) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 9px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-mute);
  }
  :global(.tps-block__title) {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }
  :global(.tps-block__actions) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  :global(.tps-none) {
    padding: 10px 14px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 20px;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  :global(.tps-row) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 6px 10px;
    padding: 9px 14px;
  }
  :global(.tps-row + .tps-row) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }
  :global(.tps-row__main) {
    flex: 1 1 220px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  :global(.tps-row__addr) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 19px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  :global(.tps-row__note) {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 3px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    line-height: 17px;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  :global(.tps-row__side) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  :global(.tps-forces) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 5px;
    margin-top: 5px;
  }
  :global(.tps-force) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-warning-soft);
    color: var(--color-warning-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 17px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  :global(.tps-badge) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-canvas-soft-2);
    color: var(--color-body);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.tps-badge--add) {
    background: var(--color-brand-soft);
    color: var(--color-brand-strong);
  }
  :global(.tps-badge--change) {
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    color: var(--color-accent-ink);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-accent-ink);
  }
  :global(.tps-badge--destroy) {
    background: var(--color-error-soft);
    color: var(--color-error-deep);
  }
  :global(.tps-badge--replace) {
    background: var(--color-warning-soft);
    color: var(--color-warning-deep);
  }

  /* ── Runtime-injected: reconciliation + notes ────────────────────────── */
  :global(.tps-note) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 9px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 19px;
    color: var(--color-body);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  :global(.tps-note + .tps-note) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }
  :global(.tps-note--error) {
    background: var(--color-error-soft);
    color: var(--color-error-deep);
  }
  :global(.tps-note--warning) {
    background: var(--color-warning-soft);
    color: var(--color-warning-deep);
  }
  :global(.tps-note--ok) {
    background: var(--color-brand-soft);
    color: var(--color-brand-strong);
  }
  :global(.tps-note__icon) {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  /* ── Runtime-injected: the dark-stable high-risk slab ────────────────── */
  :global(.tps-risk) {
    margin-top: 12px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-inverse);
    color: var(--color-inverse-fg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  :global(.tps-risk__head) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 11px 14px 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-cyan);
  }
  :global(.tps-risk__lead) {
    padding: 0 14px 10px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 19px;
    color: var(--color-inverse-fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  :global(.tps-risk__row) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 6px 10px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.14);
  }
  :global(.tps-risk__addr) {
    flex: 1 1 220px;
    min-width: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 19px;
    color: var(--color-inverse-fg);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  :global(.tps-risk__why) {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 3px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 18px;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--color-inverse-fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  :global(.tps-risk__class) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-cyan);
    color: var(--color-cyan);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.tps-risk .tps-copy) {
    color: var(--color-inverse-fg);
  }
  :global(.tps-risk .tps-copy:hover) {
    color: var(--color-cyan);
    background: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.14);
  }

  /* ── Hard error card + empty state ──────────────────────────────────── */
  :global(.tps-error) {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-error-soft);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-error);
    color: var(--color-error-deep);
  }
  :global(.tps-error__icon) {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    margin-top: 1px;
  }
  :global(.tps-error__title) {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 20px;
  }
  :global(.tps-error__detail) {
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 19px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  :global(.tps-empty) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 64px;
    padding: 20px 16px;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: pretty;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
  }

  /* ── Copy buttons: two coarse-pointer tiers, matching the reference ─── */
  :global(.tps-copy) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 0.12s ease, background 0.12s ease;
  }
  :global(.tps-copy:hover) {
    color: var(--color-brand-strong);
    background: var(--color-hairline);
  }
  :global(.tps-copy:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-link);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  :global(.tps-copy--labeled) {
    width: auto;
    height: 26px;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    background: var(--color-canvas);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hairline);
    color: var(--color-body);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.tps-copy--labeled:hover) {
    color: var(--color-brand-strong);
    background: var(--color-canvas-soft);
  }
  :global(.tps-copy--copied) {
    color: var(--color-brand-strong);
    background: var(--color-brand-soft);
  }
  @media (pointer: coarse) {
    :global(.tps-copy) {
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
    }
    :global(.tps-copy--labeled) {
      width: auto;
      height: auto;
      min-height: 44px;
    }
    .tps-chip {
      min-height: 44px;
    }
    .tps-seg__btn {
      min-height: 36px;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { escapeHtml } from '../lib/escape-html';
  import { copyTextToClipboard } from '../lib/clipboard';
  import { getRestoredLastInput, recordToolLastInput, wireSnapshotUI } from '../lib/tool-state/wire';
  import { examples } from '../lib/terraform-plan-summarizer/examples';
  import type {
    PlanSummary,
    PlanTotals,
    ResourceChange,
  } from '../lib/terraform-plan-summarizer/types';

  type EngineModule = {
    summarizePlan: (input: string) => PlanSummary;
    toMarkdown: (summary: PlanSummary) => string;
    formatTerraformTotals: (totals: PlanTotals) => string;
  };

  const ROOT_SEL = '.tps-pg';
  const SLUG = 'terraform-plan-summarizer';
  const DEBOUNCE_MS = 200;
  const ERROR_HOLD_MS = 600;
  const RESET_MS = 1800;

  /**
   * Rendered rows. The engine already caps parsing at 2,000 changes, but 2,000
   * rows × a copy button each is what stalls the tab — the same lesson as
   * MAX_OVERLAP_PAIRS in cidr-checker. Every cap here carries a visible note.
   */
  const MAX_RENDERED_ROWS = 200;
  /** Module bands in "by module" grouping. */
  const MAX_RENDERED_BANDS = 40;
  /** `forces replacement` chips shown per row. */
  const MAX_RENDERED_FORCES = 8;
  /** Diagnostic rows in the notes block. */
  const MAX_RENDERED_NOTES = 12;
  /** Output-change rows. */
  const MAX_RENDERED_OUTPUTS = 40;
  /** Drift rows. */
  const MAX_RENDERED_DRIFT = 20;

  function boot(): void {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(ROOT_SEL).forEach((root) => {
      if (root.dataset.tpsWired === 'true') return;
      root.dataset.tpsWired = 'true';
      void init(root);
    });
  }

  function el<T extends HTMLElement>(root: HTMLElement, sel: string): T | null {
    return root.querySelector<T>(sel);
  }

  const ALERT_SVG =
    '<svg class="tps-error__icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 2.5L18.5 17H1.5z"></path><path d="M10 8v4"></path><path d="M10 14.6v.01"></path></svg>';
  const WARN_SVG =
    '<svg class="tps-note__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 2.5L18.5 17H1.5z"></path><path d="M10 8v4"></path><path d="M10 14.6v.01"></path></svg>';
  const INFO_SVG =
    '<svg class="tps-note__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5"></circle><path d="M10 9v4.5"></path><path d="M10 6.4v.01"></path></svg>';
  const OK_SVG =
    '<svg class="tps-note__icon" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5"></circle><path d="M6.6 10.3l2.4 2.4 4.4-5"></path></svg>';
  const COPY_ICON_SVG =
    '<svg class="tps-copy-icon" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="5" width="9" height="9" rx="1.5"/><path d="M3 11H2a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V2a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h8a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1"/></svg>';
  const CHECK_ICON_SVG =
    '<svg class="tps-check-icon hidden" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3.5 3.5L13 4.5"/></svg>';

  /** Symbol + label + explanation. Colour never carries meaning on its own. */
  const STAT_TILES = [
    { key: 'create', cls: 'add', symbol: '+', label: 'add', sub: 'created outright' },
    { key: 'update', cls: 'change', symbol: '~', label: 'change', sub: 'updated in place' },
    { key: 'destroy', cls: 'destroy', symbol: '−', label: 'destroy', sub: 'destroyed outright' },
    {
      key: 'replace',
      cls: 'replace',
      symbol: '±',
      label: 'replace',
      sub: 'destroyed and recreated',
    },
  ] as const;

  const ACTION_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
    create: 'create',
    update: 'update',
    delete: 'destroy',
    replace: 'replace',
    read: 'read',
    import: 'import',
    move: 'move',
    'no-op': 'no change',
    forget: 'forget',
  };

  const ACTION_BADGE_CLASS: Record<string, string> = {
    create: 'tps-badge--add',
    update: 'tps-badge--change',
    delete: 'tps-badge--destroy',
    replace: 'tps-badge--replace',
  };

  const RISK_CLASS_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
    'data-store': 'data store',
    'egress-path': 'egress path',
    'control-plane': 'control plane',
    'crypto-key': 'encryption key',
  };

  /** Action bands, riskiest first — the default reading order. */
  const ACTION_BANDS: { title: string; actions: string[] }[] = [
    { title: 'Replacements', actions: ['replace'] },
    { title: 'Destroys', actions: ['delete'] },
    { title: 'Creates', actions: ['create'] },
    { title: 'Updates', actions: ['update'] },
    { title: 'Reads, imports, moves and forgets', actions: ['read', 'import', 'move', 'forget', 'no-op'] },
  ];

  function plural(n: number, one: string, many: string): string {
    return n === 1 ? one : many;
  }

  async function init(root: HTMLElement): Promise<void> {
    const input = el<HTMLTextAreaElement>(root, '#tps-input');
    const chipsWrap = el<HTMLElement>(root, '#tps-chips');
    const resultsBox = el<HTMLElement>(root, '#tps-results');
    const summaryEl = el<HTMLElement>(root, '#tps-summary');
    const mdBtn = el<HTMLButtonElement>(root, '#tps-copy-md');
    const copyStatus = el<HTMLElement>(root, '#tps-copy-status');
    const groupAction = el<HTMLButtonElement>(root, '#tps-group-action');
    const groupModule = el<HTMLButtonElement>(root, '#tps-group-module');
    const snapSaveBtn = el<HTMLButtonElement>(root, '#tps-snap-save');
    const snapSelect = el<HTMLSelectElement>(root, '#tps-snap-select');
    const snapDeleteBtn = el<HTMLButtonElement>(root, '#tps-snap-delete');
    if (
      !input ||
      !chipsWrap ||
      !resultsBox ||
      !summaryEl ||
      !mdBtn ||
      !copyStatus ||
      !groupAction ||
      !groupModule ||
      !snapSaveBtn ||
      !snapSelect ||
      !snapDeleteBtn
    )
      return;

    const chips = Array.from(chipsWrap.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.tps-chip'));

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* Copy plumbing                                                      */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

    // Payloads live in an array and are resolved by `data-copy-ref` at click
    // time. NOTHING untrusted is ever written into an attribute, and that is a
    // deliberate rule rather than an implementation detail:
    //
    //   1. A newline-joined list of 200 addresses does not round-trip through an
    //      HTML attribute at all.
    //   2. HTML attribute-value serialization escapes only `&`, `"` and U+00A0 —
    //      NOT `<`. So a resource address like `aws_s3_bucket.<img src=x
    //      onerror=alert(1)>` assigned to `data-copy` or echoed into an
    //      `aria-label` reappears as literal `<img` when the container's
    //      innerHTML is read back, even though `escapeHtml()` was applied on the
    //      way in. It is inert — an attribute value is never parsed as markup —
    //      but it is indistinguishable from a real escaping bug, so this file
    //      keeps every attribute static and every untrusted value in TEXT
    //      position, where `escapeHtml()` is genuinely sufficient.
    //
    // `data-copy` therefore stays present-but-empty: Layout.astro's analytics
    // listener matches on the attribute's presence, not its value.
    let payloads: string[] = [];
    /** The Markdown report behind the header button (outside `#tps-results`). */
    let markdown = '';

    function payloadFor(btn: HTMLButtonElement): string {
      const ref = btn.dataset.copyRef;
      if (ref !== undefined) return payloads[Number(ref)] ?? '';
      if (btn === mdBtn) return markdown;
      return btn.dataset.copy ?? '';
    }

    function setCopyStatus(message: string, failed: boolean): void {
      copyStatus!.textContent = message;
      copyStatus!.classList.toggle('sr-only', !failed);
      copyStatus!.classList.toggle('tps-copy-status--fail', failed);
    }

    function setCopied(btn: HTMLButtonElement, copied: boolean): void {
      btn.classList.toggle('tps-copy--copied', copied);
      btn.querySelector('.tps-copy-icon')?.classList.toggle('hidden', copied);
      btn.querySelector('.tps-check-icon')?.classList.toggle('hidden', !copied);
      const label = btn.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.tps-copy-label');
      if (label) {
        label.textContent = copied ? 'Copied' : (btn.dataset.copyLabel ?? 'Copy');
      } else if (copied) {
        btn.dataset.prevAriaLabel = btn.getAttribute('aria-label') ?? '';
        btn.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Copied');
      } else if (btn.dataset.prevAriaLabel) {
        btn.setAttribute('aria-label', btn.dataset.prevAriaLabel);
        delete btn.dataset.prevAriaLabel;
      }
    }

    async function handleCopy(btn: HTMLButtonElement): Promise<void> {
      const ok = await copyTextToClipboard(payloadFor(btn));
      if (ok) {
        setCopied(btn, true);
        setCopyStatus('Copied to clipboard.', false);
        window.clearTimeout(Number(btn.dataset.copyTimer));
        btn.dataset.copyTimer = String(
          window.setTimeout(() => {
            setCopied(btn, false);
            if (copyStatus!.textContent === 'Copied to clipboard.') setCopyStatus('', false);
          }, RESET_MS),
        );
      } else {
        setCopyStatus('Copy failed — select the value manually.', true);
      }
    }

    /**
     * An icon-only per-row copy button. `label` must be a STATIC string — never a
     * resource address — for the reason in the comment above `payloads`.
     */
    function copyBtnHtml(label: string, payload: string): string {
      const ref = payloads.push(payload) - 1;
      return (
        `<button class="tps-copy" type="button" data-copy="" data-copy-ref="${ref}" ` +
        `aria-label="${escapeHtml(label)}" title="${escapeHtml(label)}">` +
        COPY_ICON_SVG +
        CHECK_ICON_SVG +
        '</button>'
      );
    }

    /** A labeled band button. `data-copy-all` puts it in the 36px tap tier. */
    function copyAllBtnHtml(label: string, payload: string): string {
      const ref = payloads.push(payload) - 1;
      return (
        '<button class="tps-copy tps-copy--labeled" type="button" data-copy-all data-copy="" ' +
        `data-copy-ref="${ref}" data-copy-label="${escapeHtml(label)}">` +
        COPY_ICON_SVG +
        CHECK_ICON_SVG +
        `<span class="tps-copy-label">${escapeHtml(label)}</span></button>`
      );
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* Rendering                                                          */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

    function setSummary(text: string, isError: boolean): void {
      summaryEl!.textContent = text;
      summaryEl!.classList.toggle('text-error-deep', isError);
      summaryEl!.classList.toggle('text-mute', !isError);
    }

    function renderEmpty(): void {
      setSummary('', false);
      payloads = [];
      resultsBox!.innerHTML =
        '<p class="tps-empty body-sm text-mute">Paste a plan to see adds, changes, destroys and ' +
        'replacements counted separately, the replacement-forcing attributes named, and the ' +
        'totals cross-checked against Terraform&rsquo;s own summary line.</p>';
    }

    function statsHtml(summary: PlanSummary, engine: EngineModule): string {
      const tiles = STAT_TILES.map((tile) => {
        const n = summary.counts[tile.key];
        return (
          `<div class="tps-stat tps-stat--${tile.cls}">` +
          `<span class="tps-stat__n"><span class="tps-stat__sym" aria-hidden="true">${escapeHtml(tile.symbol)}</span>${n}</span>` +
          `<span class="tps-stat__label">${escapeHtml(tile.label)}</span>` +
          `<span class="tps-stat__sub">${escapeHtml(tile.sub)}</span></div>`
        );
      }).join('');

      const extras: string[] = [];
      if (summary.counts.read > 0) {
        extras.push(
          `${summary.counts.read} data ${plural(summary.counts.read, 'source', 'sources')} read during apply`,
        );
      }
      if (summary.counts.import > 0) extras.push(`${summary.counts.import} imported`);
      if (summary.counts.move > 0) extras.push(`${summary.counts.move} moved`);
      if (summary.counts.forget > 0) {
        extras.push(`${summary.counts.forget} removed from state but left in place`);
      }
      if (summary.counts.noop > 0) extras.push(`${summary.counts.noop} with no change`);

      const tfLine =
        `Terraform&rsquo;s own accounting counts each replacement once as an add <em>and</em> once ` +
        `as a destroy: ${escapeHtml(engine.formatTerraformTotals(summary.totals))}.` +
        (extras.length > 0 ? ` Outside those three: ${escapeHtml(extras.join(', '))}.` : '');

      return `<div class="tps-stats">${tiles}</div><p class="tps-tf-line">${tfLine}</p>`;
    }

    function reconciliationHtml(summary: PlanSummary): string {
      const status = summary.reconciliation.status;
      const cls =
        status === 'mismatch' ? 'tps-note--warning' : status === 'match' ? 'tps-note--ok' : '';
      const icon = status === 'mismatch' ? WARN_SVG : status === 'match' ? OK_SVG : INFO_SVG;
      const heading =
        status === 'match'
          ? 'Cross-check: reconciles'
          : status === 'mismatch'
            ? 'Cross-check: COUNT MISMATCH'
            : 'Cross-check: no summary line to compare against';
      const line =
        summary.summaryLine !== null
          ? `<span class="tps-row__note">Terraform printed: ${escapeHtml(summary.summaryLine)}</span>`
          : '';
      return (
        '<div class="tps-block">' +
        '<div class="tps-block__head"><span class="tps-block__title">Reconciliation</span>' +
        (summary.summaryLine !== null
          ? `<span class="tps-block__actions">${copyBtnHtml("Copy Terraform’s own summary line", summary.summaryLine)}</span>`
          : '') +
        '</div>' +
        `<div class="tps-note ${cls}">${icon}<span><strong>${escapeHtml(heading)}</strong> ` +
        `${escapeHtml(summary.reconciliation.message)}${line}</span></div>` +
        '</div>'
      );
    }

    function forcesHtml(change: ResourceChange): string {
      if (change.replaceReasons.length === 0 && !change.replaceReasonsTruncated) return '';
      const shown = change.replaceReasons.slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_FORCES);
      const chipsHtml = shown
        .map((attr) => `<span class="tps-force">${escapeHtml(attr)}</span>`)
        .join('');
      const hidden = change.replaceReasons.length - shown.length;
      const more =
        hidden > 0 || change.replaceReasonsTruncated
          ? `<span class="tps-force">${hidden > 0 ? `and ${hidden} more` : 'and more, not listed'}</span>`
          : '';
      return (
        '<span class="tps-row__note">forces replacement:</span>' +
        `<span class="tps-forces">${chipsHtml}${more}</span>`
      );
    }

    function rowHtml(change: ResourceChange, showModule: boolean): string {
      const notes: string[] = [];
      if (change.replaceOrder === 'destroy-create') {
        notes.push('destroy then create — the resource does not exist in between');
      } else if (change.replaceOrder === 'create-destroy') {
        notes.push('create then destroy (create_before_destroy)');
      }
      if (change.tainted) notes.push('marked tainted');
      if (change.imported) notes.push('imported into state');
      if (change.movedFrom !== null) notes.push(`moved from ${change.movedFrom}`);
      if (change.sensitive) notes.push('has attributes the plan marked sensitive');
      if (change.actionReason !== null) notes.push(change.actionReason);
      if (showModule && change.moduleChain.length > 0) {
        notes.push(`in module ${change.moduleChain.join(' › ')}`);
      }
      if (change.provider !== null) notes.push(change.provider);

      const badgeClass = ACTION_BADGE_CLASS[change.action] ?? '';
      return (
        '<div class="tps-row">' +
        '<div class="tps-row__main">' +
        `<span class="tps-row__addr">${escapeHtml(change.address)}</span>` +
        (notes.length > 0
          ? `<span class="tps-row__note">${escapeHtml(notes.join(' · '))}</span>`
          : '') +
        forcesHtml(change) +
        '</div>' +
        '<span class="tps-row__side">' +
        `<span class="tps-badge ${badgeClass}">${escapeHtml(ACTION_LABEL[change.action] ?? change.action)}</span>` +
        copyBtnHtml('Copy this resource address', change.address) +
        '</span></div>'
      );
    }

    interface Band {
      title: string;
      rows: ResourceChange[];
    }

    /**
     * Deliberately short and count-bearing rather than descriptive: the band
     * heading right next to it already says which addresses these are, and a
     * `white-space: nowrap` label like "Copy reads, imports, moves and forgets
     * addresses" is 310px wide, which overflows a 390px viewport.
     */
    function addressCopyLabel(n: number): string {
      return n === 1 ? 'Copy the address' : `Copy the ${n} addresses`;
    }

    function bandsFor(summary: PlanSummary, grouping: 'action' | 'module'): Band[] {
      if (grouping === 'action') {
        return ACTION_BANDS.map((band) => ({
          title: band.title,
          rows: summary.changes.filter((change) => band.actions.includes(change.action)),
        })).filter((band) => band.rows.length > 0);
      }
      const groups = new Map<string, ResourceChange[]>();
      for (const change of summary.changes) {
        const key = change.moduleChain.length === 0 ? '' : change.moduleChain.join('.');
        const list = groups.get(key);
        if (list) list.push(change);
        else groups.set(key, [change]);
      }
      return Array.from(groups.entries()).map(([key, rows]) => ({
        title: key === '' ? 'Root module' : `module ${key.split('.').join(' › ')}`,
        rows,
      }));
    }

    function bandsHtml(summary: PlanSummary, grouping: 'action' | 'module'): string {
      const all = bandsFor(summary, grouping);
      const bands = all.slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_BANDS);
      let budget = MAX_RENDERED_ROWS;
      let dropped = 0;
      const html: string[] = [];

      for (const band of bands) {
        const shown = band.rows.slice(0, Math.max(0, budget));
        dropped += band.rows.length - shown.length;
        budget -= shown.length;
        const addresses = band.rows.map((change) => change.address).join('\n');
        html.push(
          '<div class="tps-block">' +
            '<div class="tps-block__head">' +
            `<span class="tps-block__title">${escapeHtml(band.title)} · ${band.rows.length}</span>` +
            `<span class="tps-block__actions">${copyAllBtnHtml(addressCopyLabel(band.rows.length), addresses)}</span>` +
            '</div>' +
            shown.map((change) => rowHtml(change, grouping === 'action')).join('') +
            (shown.length < band.rows.length
              ? `<p class="tps-none">Showing ${shown.length} of ${band.rows.length} rows in this group. The copy button above still copies every address.</p>`
              : '') +
            '</div>',
        );
      }

      if (all.length > bands.length) {
        html.push(
          `<p class="tps-none">Showing the first ${bands.length} of ${all.length} groups. Copy the Markdown summary for the whole plan.</p>`,
        );
      } else if (dropped > 0) {
        html.push(
          `<p class="tps-none">${dropped} further ${plural(dropped, 'row was', 'rows were')} not rendered, to keep this page responsive.</p>`,
        );
      }
      return html.join('');
    }

    function riskHtml(summary: PlanSummary): string {
      if (summary.highRisk.length === 0) return '';
      const shown = summary.highRisk.slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_ROWS);
      const rows = shown
        .map(
          (change) =>
            '<div class="tps-risk__row">' +
            `<span class="tps-risk__addr">${escapeHtml(change.address)}` +
            `<span class="tps-risk__why">${escapeHtml(change.risk!.reason)}</span></span>` +
            '<span class="tps-row__side">' +
            `<span class="tps-risk__class">${escapeHtml(RISK_CLASS_LABEL[change.risk!.klass] ?? change.risk!.klass)}</span>` +
            copyBtnHtml('Copy this resource address', change.address) +
            '</span></div>',
        )
        .join('');
      const addresses = summary.highRisk.map((change) => change.address).join('\n');
      const n = summary.highRisk.length;
      return (
        '<div class="tps-risk">' +
        `<div class="tps-risk__head"><span>Read this first · ${n} high blast radius</span>` +
        `<span class="tps-block__actions">${copyAllBtnHtml(addressCopyLabel(n), addresses)}</span></div>` +
        `<p class="tps-risk__lead">${n} destructive ${plural(n, 'action', 'actions')} ` +
        'in this plan hits a resource type that holds data, carries your egress path, or is a ' +
        'cluster control plane. A type that is <em>not</em> listed here is unclassified, not ' +
        'proven safe — nobody can enumerate every provider&rsquo;s stateful resources.</p>' +
        rows +
        '</div>'
      );
    }

    function outputsHtml(summary: PlanSummary): string {
      if (summary.outputChanges.length === 0) return '';
      const shown = summary.outputChanges.slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_OUTPUTS);
      const rows = shown
        .map((output) => {
          const badge =
            output.action === 'create'
              ? 'tps-badge--add'
              : output.action === 'delete'
                ? 'tps-badge--destroy'
                : output.action === 'update'
                  ? 'tps-badge--change'
                  : '';
          return (
            '<div class="tps-row"><div class="tps-row__main">' +
            `<span class="tps-row__addr">${escapeHtml(output.name)}</span>` +
            (output.sensitive
              ? '<span class="tps-row__note">marked sensitive — the value is not printed in the plan</span>'
              : '') +
            '</div><span class="tps-row__side">' +
            `<span class="tps-badge ${badge}">${escapeHtml(output.action === 'delete' ? 'destroy' : output.action)}</span>` +
            copyBtnHtml('Copy this output name', output.name) +
            '</span></div>'
          );
        })
        .join('');
      return (
        '<div class="tps-block"><div class="tps-block__head">' +
        `<span class="tps-block__title">Output changes · ${summary.outputChanges.length}</span></div>` +
        rows +
        (shown.length < summary.outputChanges.length
          ? `<p class="tps-none">Showing ${shown.length} of ${summary.outputChanges.length} outputs.</p>`
          : '') +
        '</div>'
      );
    }

    function driftHtml(summary: PlanSummary): string {
      if (summary.drift.length === 0) return '';
      const shown = summary.drift.slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_DRIFT);
      const rows = shown
        .map(
          (change) =>
            '<div class="tps-row"><div class="tps-row__main">' +
            `<span class="tps-row__addr">${escapeHtml(change.address)}</span></div>` +
            '<span class="tps-row__side">' +
            copyBtnHtml('Copy this resource address', change.address) +
            '</span></div>',
        )
        .join('');
      return (
        '<div class="tps-block"><div class="tps-block__head">' +
        `<span class="tps-block__title">Changed outside Terraform · ${summary.drift.length}</span></div>` +
        '<p class="tps-none">Drift: Terraform found these already different from the last state it ' +
        'recorded. They are NOT part of the counts above.</p>' +
        rows +
        (shown.length < summary.drift.length
          ? `<p class="tps-none">Showing ${shown.length} of ${summary.drift.length}.</p>`
          : '') +
        '</div>'
      );
    }

    function notesHtml(summary: PlanSummary): string {
      const notes = summary.diagnostics.filter(
        (diagnostic) => diagnostic.message !== summary.reconciliation.message,
      );
      if (notes.length === 0) return '';
      const shown = notes.slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_NOTES);
      const rows = shown
        .map((diagnostic) => {
          const icon =
            diagnostic.severity === 'info'
              ? INFO_SVG
              : WARN_SVG;
          return (
            `<div class="tps-note tps-note--${escapeHtml(diagnostic.severity)}">${icon}` +
            `<span>${escapeHtml(diagnostic.message)}</span></div>`
          );
        })
        .join('');
      return (
        '<div class="tps-block"><div class="tps-block__head">' +
        `<span class="tps-block__title">Notes · ${notes.length}</span></div>` +
        rows +
        (shown.length < notes.length
          ? `<p class="tps-none">…and ${notes.length - shown.length} more, not shown.</p>`
          : '') +
        '</div>'
      );
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* Engine                                                             */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

    let engine: EngineModule;
    try {
      engine = (await import('../lib/terraform-plan-summarizer/engine')) as unknown as EngineModule;
    } catch (err) {
      setSummary('', true);
      resultsBox.innerHTML =
        '<div class="tps-error" role="alert">' +
        ALERT_SVG +
        '<div><p class="tps-error__title">Summarizer unavailable</p>' +
        '<p class="tps-error__detail">The plan engine failed to load. Reload the page to try ' +
        'again — nothing you pasted was sent anywhere.</p></div></div>';
      console.error('[TerraformPlanSummarizer] engine import failed:', err);
      return;
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* State machine: EMPTY | VALID | PENDING | INVALID                   */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

    type State = 'empty' | 'valid' | 'pending' | 'invalid';
    let state: State = 'empty';
    /** Previous textarea value, so one `input` event's delta can be measured. */
    let prevValue = input.value;
    let evalTimer: number | undefined;
    let errTimer: number | undefined;
    let grouping: 'action' | 'module' = 'action';
    /** The last valid summary, so the grouping toggle re-renders without reparsing. */
    let lastSummary: PlanSummary | null = null;

    function clearTimers(): void {
      window.clearTimeout(evalTimer);
      window.clearTimeout(errTimer);
    }

    function setErrorState(on: boolean): void {
      input!.classList.toggle('tps-input--error', on);
      if (on) {
        input!.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
        input!.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'tps-input-hint tps-run-hint tps-error-detail');
      } else {
        input!.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
        input!.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'tps-input-hint tps-run-hint');
      }
    }

    function hideActions(): void {
      mdBtn!.hidden = true;
      markdown = '';
    }

    function setActiveChip(idx: number | null): void {
      chips.forEach((chip) => {
        chip.setAttribute(
          'aria-pressed',
          idx !== null && chip.dataset.exampleIdx === String(idx) ? 'true' : 'false',
        );
      });
    }

    function toEmpty(): void {
      state = 'empty';
      clearTimers();
      lastSummary = null;
      setErrorState(false);
      hideActions();
      renderEmpty();
      setActiveChip(null);
    }

    /** The hard-error card: shown when nothing usable was found at all. */
    function showError(summary: PlanSummary, isAlert: boolean): void {
      state = 'invalid';
      clearTimers();
      lastSummary = null;
      setErrorState(true);
      hideActions();
      payloads = [];
      const worst =
        summary.diagnostics.find((d) => d.severity === 'error') ??
        summary.diagnostics.find((d) => d.severity === 'warning') ??
        summary.diagnostics[0];
      const others = summary.diagnostics.filter((d) => d !== worst);
      setSummary('nothing to summarize', true);
      resultsBox!.innerHTML =
        `<div class="tps-error"${isAlert ? ' role="alert"' : ''}>` +
        ALERT_SVG +
        '<div><p class="tps-error__title">No plan to summarize yet</p>' +
        `<p id="tps-error-detail" class="tps-error__detail">${escapeHtml(worst?.message ?? '')}</p>` +
        '</div></div>' +
        (others.length > 0
          ? '<div class="tps-block"><div class="tps-block__head"><span class="tps-block__title">Also noticed</span></div>' +
            others
              .slice(0, MAX_RENDERED_NOTES)
              .map(
                (d) =>
                  `<div class="tps-note tps-note--${escapeHtml(d.severity)}">${d.severity === 'info' ? INFO_SVG : WARN_SVG}<span>${escapeHtml(d.message)}</span></div>`,
              )
              .join('') +
            '</div>'
          : '');
    }

    function renderSummary(summary: PlanSummary): void {
      payloads = [];
      const body = summary.noChanges
        ? '<div class="tps-block"><div class="tps-block__head"><span class="tps-block__title">No changes</span></div>' +
          '<p class="tps-none">Terraform found nothing to do: your configuration and the real ' +
          'infrastructure already agree. Nothing will be created, changed or destroyed.</p></div>'
        : statsHtml(summary, engine) + riskHtml(summary) + bandsHtml(summary, grouping);

      resultsBox!.innerHTML =
        body +
        reconciliationHtml(summary) +
        outputsHtml(summary) +
        driftHtml(summary) +
        notesHtml(summary);

      const statusBits = [
        summary.format === 'json' ? 'show -json' : 'plan text',
        summary.noChanges
          ? 'no changes'
          : `${summary.stats.changes} ${plural(summary.stats.changes, 'action', 'actions')}`,
      ];
      if (summary.highRisk.length > 0) statusBits.push(`${summary.highRisk.length} high risk`);
      statusBits.push(
        summary.reconciliation.status === 'match'
          ? 'counts reconcile'
          : summary.reconciliation.status === 'mismatch'
            ? 'COUNT MISMATCH'
            : 'no cross-check',
      );
      setSummary(statusBits.join(' · '), summary.reconciliation.status === 'mismatch');

      markdown = engine.toMarkdown(summary);
      mdBtn!.hidden = false;
    }

    function evaluate(source: 'type' | 'bulk' | 'commit' | 'seed'): void {
      clearTimers();
      const value = input!.value;
      prevValue = value;
      if (value.trim().length === 0) {
        toEmpty();
        return;
      }

      const summary = engine.summarizePlan(value);

      if (summary.ok) {
        state = 'valid';
        setErrorState(false);
        lastSummary = summary;
        renderSummary(summary);
        // Only a fully valid, user-initiated evaluation is allowed to persist.
        // A seeded boot must never write, and neither must a partial paste:
        // poisoning `oc-last-v1` makes the NEXT visit boot broken. There is no
        // deep-link hash for this tool, so nothing else is written either.
        if (source !== 'seed') recordToolLastInput(SLUG, value);
        return;
      }

      if (source !== 'type') {
        showError(summary, source === 'commit');
        return;
      }

      // Mid-typing: hold the error. No red border, no error card — keep whatever
      // is on screen until the person stops typing for ERROR_HOLD_MS.
      const wasInvalid = state === 'invalid';
      state = 'pending';
      setErrorState(false);
      hideActions();
      setSummary('', false);
      if (wasInvalid) {
        payloads = [];
        resultsBox!.innerHTML =
          '<p class="tps-empty body-sm text-mute">Still typing — results appear once there is a ' +
          'plan to read.</p>';
      }
      errTimer = window.setTimeout(() => showError(summary, false), ERROR_HOLD_MS);
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* Events                                                             */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

    function setGrouping(next: 'action' | 'module'): void {
      if (grouping === next) return;
      grouping = next;
      groupAction!.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(next === 'action'));
      groupAction!.tabIndex = next === 'action' ? 0 : -1;
      groupModule!.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(next === 'module'));
      groupModule!.tabIndex = next === 'module' ? 0 : -1;
      // Re-render from the summary already in hand: regrouping is a view change,
      // not a new evaluation, so it must not re-persist the last input either.
      if (lastSummary !== null) renderSummary(lastSummary);
    }

    root.addEventListener('click', (evt) => {
      const target = evt.target as HTMLElement;

      const chip = target.closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.tps-chip');
      if (chip && chipsWrap!.contains(chip)) {
        const idx = Number(chip.dataset.exampleIdx);
        const example = examples[idx];
        if (!example) return;
        input!.value = example.input;
        prevValue = example.input;
        setActiveChip(idx);
        evaluate('commit');
        return;
      }

      const seg = target.closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.tps-seg__btn');
      if (seg) {
        setGrouping(seg.id === 'tps-group-module' ? 'module' : 'action');
        return;
      }

      const copy = target.closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.tps-copy');
      if (copy) void handleCopy(copy);
    });

    // Arrow keys move within a radiogroup, per the ARIA pattern.
    root.addEventListener('keydown', (evt) => {
      const seg = (evt.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('.tps-seg__btn');
      if (!seg) return;
      if (evt.key !== 'ArrowLeft' && evt.key !== 'ArrowRight') return;
      evt.preventDefault();
      const next = grouping === 'action' ? 'module' : 'action';
      setGrouping(next);
      (next === 'module' ? groupModule! : groupAction!).focus();
    });

    input.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
      clearTimers();
      const value = input.value;
      // Only GROWTH beyond one character is a paste. `Math.abs(delta) > 1` would
      // treat a backspace over a selection as a paste, flash a red border
      // mid-edit, and break the calm-error contract. Deletions and IME
      // composition debounce like typing.
      const grew = value.length - prevValue.length > 1;
      const composing = (e as InputEvent).isComposing === true;
      prevValue = value;
      setActiveChip(null);
      if (value.trim().length === 0) {
        toEmpty();
        return;
      }
      if (grew && !composing) {
        evaluate('bulk');
        return;
      }
      evalTimer = window.setTimeout(() => evaluate('type'), DEBOUNCE_MS);
    });

    input.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key !== 'Enter') return;
      if (e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) {
        e.preventDefault();
        evaluate('commit');
        if (window.matchMedia?.('(pointer: coarse)').matches) input.blur();
        return;
      }
      // Plain Enter must still insert the newline — a plan is multi-line. Flush
      // on the next tick, once the textarea value includes it.
      window.setTimeout(() => evaluate('commit'), 0);
    });

    input.addEventListener('blur', () => {
      if (state === 'pending') evaluate('commit');
    });

    wireSnapshotUI({
      slug: SLUG,
      saveBtn: snapSaveBtn,
      snapshotSelect: snapSelect,
      deleteBtn: snapDeleteBtn,
      getValue: () => input!.value,
      setValue: (value) => {
        input!.value = value;
        prevValue = value;
        setActiveChip(null);
        evaluate('commit');
      },
    });

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /* First load: typed value → restored last input → first example.     */
    /* There is NO deep link for this tool (a plan is orders of magnitude  */
    /* past the fragment cap), so nothing here reads or writes            */
    /* location.hash — including an unknown key someone appends by hand.   */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

    const restored = getRestoredLastInput(SLUG);
    if (input.value.trim()) {
      evaluate('seed');
    } else if (restored) {
      input.value = restored;
      prevValue = restored;
      evaluate('seed');
    } else if (examples[0]) {
      input.value = examples[0].input;
      prevValue = examples[0].input;
      setActiveChip(0);
      evaluate('seed');
    } else {
      renderEmpty();
    }
  }

  boot();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', boot);
</script>
